From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 09:02:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/62] verimark: handshake orchestrator becomes IT-aware
 (is_it_variant flag)

Adds a bool is_it_variant parameter to verimark_handshake_perform()
(sync) and verimark_handshake_perform_async() so the orchestrator
can advertise the IT-specific 5-cipher ClientHello when needed,
without duplicating the ~500-LOC handshake machinery. The flag is
stored on HandshakeAsyncCtx for the async path.

Branching at the two existing build_client_hello call sites:

    ch_n = is_it_variant
        ? verimark_tls_build_client_hello_it(...)   // 78 B, 5 ciphers
        : verimark_tls_build_client_hello(...);     // 80 B, 6 ciphers

All other handshake steps (ServerHello parse, cipher check against
0xc02e, cert/CKE/CV/CCS/Finished build, AES-256-GCM, KDF) are
shared verbatim with the DT path: the runtime end-to-end validation
of voie A on 2026-06-07 proved the IT firmware accepts the same
cipher + KDF + format as the DT, so reusing the orchestrator is
correct.

Callers updated to pass false (DT path preserved bit-for-bit):
- verimark.c: open() first attempt + stale-state recovery retry
- tests/test_handshake.c: 7 existing sync calls

New TDD test first_write_is_expected_client_hello_it_variant
asserts that when is_it_variant=true:
- the wire is the byte-for-byte IT ClientHello (78 B)
- is_handshake=true is still set on the transport (44 00 00 00
  prefix still applied)

All 12 standalone tests green (was 12, now 12 with 1 new IT
assertion folded into test_handshake).
